# Line endings: text is stored AND checked out as LF, everywhere.
#
# Why this exists. Every tool in this repo emits and expects LF — prettier,
# rustfmt, eslint, vitest. Without a policy the index held LF while a Windows
# checkout produced CRLF, so the same file was clean for one tool and dirty for
# another: local format checks disagreed with CI, a literal multi-line search
# failed on a file that looked normal, and an agent rewriting three files
# LF->CRLF inflated a one-line change into 656 lines of diff.
#
# This rule sits ABOVE the binary list on purpose. The last matching pattern
# wins, and `binary` sets -text, which disables the conversion, so the binaries
# below stay untouched no matter what this line says.
#
# Windows-native scripts (gradlew.bat, scripts/e2e/*.ps1) are deliberately not
# exempted: they are already LF in the index and working tree, cmd.exe runs them
# that way, and adding a CRLF rule would only create churn.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files — never normalize line endings (protects encrypted .pen designs and assets)
*.pen binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.apk binary
*.pdf binary
